# Boron 2P with its p electron in the complex m=+1 orbital, without a
# field. Its LDA energy differs from that of the real p_x state that
# erkale would give (-24.34874), by 0.89 mEh.
System B.xyz
Basis cc-pVDZ
Method lda_x-lda_c_vwn
Multiplicity 2
Restricted false
ComplexBasis true
LinearOccupations -1
LinearOccupationFile complex_orbs_b_ml.linocc
LinearB 0.0
JKMethod Cholesky
DFTGrid 75 -302
ConvThr 1e-9
SaveChk complex_orbs_b_ml_0.chk
